{
  "description": "Phoneme tags say what a token sounds like. A token keeps its phonemes as they are, and phonemes() of a later stage reads them in canonical form, in lower case (engine §5).",
  "documents": {
    "p.md": "## s\n\n```jbogenbau\n%stage sounds\n```\n\n- [g](g.md)\n  ```jbogenbau\n  %include \"g.md\"\n  ```\n\n## t\n\n```jbogenbau\n%stage words\n```\n\n- [h](h.md)\n  ```jbogenbau\n  %include \"h.md\"\n  ```\n",
    "g.md": "```jbogenbau\n%ambiguity-resolution greedy\n%rule text [{c}]\n%rule c 'a' </a/> | 'Á' </A/> | '\\p{White_Space}' </./> %emits $\n```\n",
    "h.md": "```jbogenbau\n%ambiguity-resolution greedy\n%rule text $w(pair) %conditions phonemes($w) = \"aa\"\n%rule pair /a/ /A/\n```\n"
  },
  "pipeline": "p.md",
  "input": "aÁ",
  "expect": {
    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stages": [
        {
          "output": [
            {
              "text": "a",
              "phonemes": "a"
            },
            {
              "text": "Á",
              "phonemes": "A"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "verdict": "unique"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
